  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/cdefb8ca-6cfb-4431-be57-306b2e23aee9-8525a8ca-bf38-4117-8ee9-7d0ffa5ab1ed-image.png\" style=\"width: 728px; height: 294px;\" /></p><p>The substance produce by ants is formic acid, which is the product of oxidation of &quot;a&quot;, means &#39;a&#39; should be formaldehyde. Now, formaldehyde and ketons are prepared by reductive&nbsp;ozonolysis of alkenes. And by oxidation in presence of strong oxidising agents alkenes give ketons and acids.</p></blockquote>",
